A||||13||frontal lobe||Royalty for a day, part  II||||1||
Z||000000||frontal lobe||10-04-2001||02:39 PM||||So I was at the Pontiac dealership today because I needed to get the radio adapter harness thingy to put in a new radio that works instead of my old, broken unit.  Well, the owner is a personal friend of mine.  He says, come over here, I have a car I want to show you and when it's a nice day you can drive it (it's raining today).  So he takes me over to one of those Shelby Cobra cars.  4.0 northstar with 325 h.p.  Says they come with a supercharged model with 510 h.p.  Only weighs 2600 pounds!  Says he has driven the base model at Elkhart at 165 m.p.h.!  Says the supercharged model does &gt;200 but he hasn't driven one that fast!  Price-$140,000 to 210,000.  So obviously WAY out of my league, and priced only for the "beautiful people".  But still, he says I can drive it on a nice day, just say the word.<P>Should I do it??||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||10-04-2001||03:16 PM||||Well why wouldn't you?||||reg||1
Z||000002||onfire||10-04-2001||04:10 PM||||You have to ask? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <BR>Just make sure it's insured.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||10-04-2001||08:59 PM||||Drive it,just don't sign any papers without a lawyer checking them first.You're liable to be buying it!||||reg||14
Z||000004||p4n1c||10-04-2001||09:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>So he takes me over to one of those Shelby Cobra cars.  4.0 northstar with 325 h.p.  Says they come with a supercharged model with 510 h.p.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Excuse my ignorance, but wasn't the Cobra a joint venture between Oldsmobile and Shelby?  So wouldn't that make it a 4.0 Aurora engine?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jake_Dragon||10-04-2001||09:48 PM||||The only problem I see is finding your way back to the dealer.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"><B>1985 GT</B></FONT><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||frontal lobe||10-05-2001||12:16 AM||||Oops.  Yes, it was a joint venture with Oldsmobile.  It is the 4.0 from the Aurora but with modifications for this program.  Do some people call that engine the "shortstar"?<P>Why not drive it?  Well on the surface you would think why not?  But, you know, what am I supposed to wear???  Armani suit?  Gold chain with snaggle tooth?  Should I get my hair cut?  <P>And what if I'm at a stop light on a 4-lane and someone pulls up next to me and says,"Nice car."  Do I look over the top of my Foster Grants and snub the person?  <P>If I'm going to drive like the royalty, how am I supposed to act?  Otherwise, I'm just the automotive version of the Beverly Hillbillies.  I never realized how much pressure it is to be one of the rich and famous, beautiful people.||||reg||1
Z||000007||hugh||10-05-2001||07:05 AM||||Don't shave for a few days(if possible),dress like the Clampetts and act normal.I bet you don't get past the first cop!||||reg||1
Z||000008||bHooper||10-05-2001||08:31 AM||||hugh, you beat me to it.  i was going to suggest you wear your greasy "working on the car" shirt (cleaned of course but still stained). <P>that would make a nice impresion, but then again people may just think your the mechanic.<P>so, that said... <B>DRIVE NAKED</B> with the top down!<P>good luck, have fun!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||10-05-2001||09:28 AM||||Wear a pair of Oakleys and a sleeveless t-shirt (Is it still warm enough, up there?). And a baseball cap with a logo for some sort of heavy equipment. <BR>The look you're after is "Dale" from "King of the Hill".<P>"The name's ummmm.... Rusty Shackleford" -Dale<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||frontal lobe||10-05-2001||02:58 PM||||If I'm going with the Oakleys and the sleeveless shirt, then I'm going to need a temporary tattoo for the deltoid area, preferably one that will look good with goosebumps, because it's down in the high 40's already.||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||10-06-2001||05:19 AM||||Think "Al Bundie" heh.  (or hop in withought pants, see if anyone notices)<P>That's a Shelby Series 1.  His ''cobra" for the 21st centuary.  Very nice, very nice indeed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(It's indeed an Aurora V8, which ***IS*** a Northstar V8 with only a smaller bore, and different intake.  Awesome engine in either guise.<P>PS: Act like the guy I 'met' in an Esprit the other night, and like most Ferrari drivers I know.  Be kind, friendly, wave a lot, give other people thumbs-up, smile and do burnouts for children who ask nicely!<P>Drive it like you stole it.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||Steve Normington||10-06-2001||10:01 AM||||Don't forget, if you're going to drive a car like that, you need a hot babe for the passanger seat (at least a 9). The kind of woman that says, "I'm with him only for the money."||||reg||1
Z||000013||frontal lobe||10-06-2001||10:44 PM||||Steve,<P>Oh yeah, how could I forget that??  And I'm 45 so I figure, what, about 20 years younger than me should do, right?  And my forehead is up to about a 5-head, so should I get a really bad toupee, but then it's a convertible so I don't know.<P>Art,<P>Some excellent advice there!<BR>Yeah, I didn't know if the Aurora engine shared the Northstar family name or not.||||reg||1
